# Force LF line endings for these files regardless of any contributor's or
# cloner's local core.autocrlf setting. This matters for more than style:
# shell scripts here are meant to run on Kali Linux — a CRLF shebang line
# (#!/bin/bash\r) makes Linux's script loader look for a "/bin/bash\r"
# interpreter that doesn't exist, so the script fails outright with
# "bad interpreter" rather than just looking odd in a diff. It also keeps
# LF-anchored parsing (agent-spec verification tooling, README phase
# parsing) working the same for every contributor.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf

# Binary/asset files — never touch line endings
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
